#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Result metadata {#result-metadata}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to the execution results, both the `PrimitiveResult` and "
"`SamplerPubResult` objects contain a metadata attribute about the job that "
"was submitted. The metadata containing information for all submitted PUBs "
"(such as the various [runtime "
"options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options) "
"available) can be found in the `PrimitiveResult.metatada`, while the "
"metadata specific to each PUB is found in `SamplerPubResult.metadata`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The client-side Sampler submits its workload as an "
"[Executor](/guides/executor-input-output) job. The metadata of the "
"underlying Executor result, which includes execution timing information "
"called [_execution spans_](#execution-spans), is available under the "
"`\"executor\"` key of `PrimitiveResult.metadata`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"In the metadata field, primitive implementations can return any information about execution that is relevant to them, and there are no key-value pairs that are guaranteed by the base primitive. Thus, the returned metadata might be different in different primitive implementations.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"execution-spans\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "View execution spans {#view-execution-spans}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The client-side Sampler uses Executor to run jobs, which executes its work "
"on the QPU in _chunks_. The timing of each chunk is in "
"`result.metadata[\"executor\"].chunk_timing`, a list of "
"[`ChunkSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/results-"
"chunk-span) objects. Each `ChunkSpan` has `start` and `stop` timestamps and "
"a list of `parts`, where each part gives an item index (`idx_item`) and the "
"number of configurations from that item (`size`) that ran in the chunk.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sampler creates one Executor program item per PUB, so `idx_item` is the "
"index of the PUB, in the order the PUBs were given to `run()`. If twirling "
"is enabled, each randomization of each parameter value set counts as a "
"separate configuration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To visualize the timings, pass the list to "
"[`draw_chunk_timings`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/visualization-draw-chunk-timings), as shown in the following "
"example.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To learn what the chunk timestamps mean, how to read the plot, and why gaps "
"can appear between chunks, see [View execution spans](/guides/executor-"
"input-output#execution-spans) in the Executor inputs and outputs guide.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"legacy-execution-spans\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Execution spans in the legacy Sampler {#execution-spans-in-the-legacy-"
"sampler}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As of `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, the legacy server-side Sampler is "
"deprecated. The client-side Sampler does not return `ExecutionSpans` "
"objects; use the [chunk timing](#execution-spans) described previously "
"instead. See [Migrate to client-side primitives](/guides/migrate-to-client-"
"side-primitives) for instructions to migrate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"**Click to learn more.**\">\n"
"    The results of jobs from the legacy server-side [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) contain execution timing information in `result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]`, in the form of an [`ExecutionSpans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-spans) object. This object is a list-like container of [`ExecutionSpan`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/execution-span-execution-span) objects, each of which indicates a start time, a stop time, and a specification of which shots were collected in the span.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    An execution span specifies which data was executed during its window by"
" providing an "
"[`ExecutionSpan.mask`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/execution-span-execution-span#mask) method. This method, given any "
"PUB index, returns a boolean mask that is `True` for all shots executed "
"during its window. If, for example, a PUB has shape `(2, 3)` and was run "
"with four shots, then the mask's shape is `(2, 3, 4)`. See the "
"[execution_span](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/execution-span) API page for full details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python noexec\n"
"    from qiskit.primitives import BitArray\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    spans = result.metadata[\"execution\"][\"execution_spans\"]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Get the mask of the 1st PUB for the 0th span.\n"
"    mask = spans[0].mask(0)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Create a new bit array containing only the PUB-0 data collected during this span.\n"
"    bits = result[0].data.meas\n"
"    filtered_data = BitArray(bits.array[mask], bits.num_bits)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Take the subset of spans that reference data in PUBs 0 or 2\n"
"    spans.filter_by_pub([0, 2])\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # View global information about the collection of execution spans\n"
"    print(\"Number of execution spans:\", len(spans))\n"
"    print(\"  Start of the first span:\", spans.start)\n"
"    print(\"     End of the last span:\", spans.stop)\n"
"    print(\"       Total duration (s):\", spans.duration)\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    To visualize legacy execution spans, use the "
"[`draw_execution_spans`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/visualization-draw-execution-spans) function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    It is possible for time windows specified by distinct execution spans to overlap. This is not because a QPU was performing multiple executions simultaneously, but is instead an artifact of certain classical processing that might happen concurrently with quantum execution. The guarantee is that the referenced data definitely occurred in the reported execution span, but not necessarily that the limits of the time window are as tight as possible.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
